From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:07:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(browse): unify compact glass header and scroll boundaries

Address added user feedback: source browse header height and glass differ from library, and fast return to the beginning does not commit revealed navigation. Remove opaque source/global-search wrapper colors under browsing chrome; keep solid fallback outside that context. Compact source headers place the existing horizontally scrollable popular/latest/filter/saved-search controls between source title and actions, including Anikku selection count; keep search input width and animate the separate shared-height filter row when needed. Retain filter scroll state and all existing actions. Route native source lists and regular grids through the same fast-scroll components as the library, preserving paging, sizing and selection. Both leading and trailing edge observations commit shared visibility after content/programmatic returns, preventing an old hidden target from reappearing after leaving the spacer. Add three real Compose compact-header/filter-reachability and list/grid first-row regression tests. Fix only the first-attempt sheet test locator to use the actual unmerged scroll node under the clickable surface; distance, velocity and callback assertions remain unchanged.
